==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|rogen|lang=gmh}} and {{term|roge|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|rogan|lang=goh}}, {{term|rogin|lang=goh}}, {{term/t|goh|*hrogan}} and {{term|rogo||roe|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hrugnaz}} and {{term/t|gem-pro|*hrugô||roe}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*krek-||frogspawn}}. Compare Low German {{term|Rögen|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|roge|lang=nl}}, English {{term|roe|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|rogn|lang=da}}. More at {{l|en|roe}}.

